\label{lem:semiring}
The stated identifications form a semigroup congruence. The quotient is
$0$-cancellative, and $B(\mathcal H)$ is a finite commutative ai-semiring.

\label{thm:local}
Let $n\geqslant1$. Under the assumptions of the preceding section, if
\begin{equation}\label{eq:localbound}
 k>n(d-1),
\end{equation}
then every subsemiring of $B(\mathcal H)$ generated by at most $n$ elements
belongs to $\mathcal N$.

\label{cor:boundedsizevarieties}
For every $r\geqslant3$, the variety $\mathcal U_r$ generated by all
ai-semirings of cardinality at most $r$ has infinite axiomatic rank.

\label{cor:exactorder}
Let $\mathcal T_r$ be the variety generated by all ai-semirings of
cardinality exactly $r$. Then $\mathcal T_r=\mathcal U_r$ for every
$r\geqslant1$. This variety is finitely based if and only if $r\leqslant2$;
for every $r\geqslant3$ it has infinite axiomatic rank.
